To give you the exact code you need, it helps to know a bit about your setup, but here are the two most common ways to do this right away:

---

### Option 1: Clean HTML & CSS (Ready to customize)
If you are building your own site with HTML/CSS, paste this code where you want the form to appear.

**HTML:**
```html
<div class="newsletter-container">
  <h3>Subscribe to our Newsletter</h3>
  <p>Get the latest updates delivered straight to your inbox.</p>

  <form class="newsletter-form" action="/subscribe" method="POST">
    <input 
      type="email" 
      name="email" 
      placeholder="Enter your email address" 
      required 
    />
    <button type="submit">Subscribe</button>
  </form>
</div>
```

**CSS:**
```css
.newsletter-container {
  max-width: 450px;
  margin: 40px auto;
  padding: 30px;
  background: #f9f9f9;
  border-radius: 8px;
  text-align: center;
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
}

.newsletter-container h3 {
  margin-top: 0;
  color: #333;
}

.newsletter-container p {
  color: #666;
  font-size: 14px;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.newsletter-form {
  display: flex;
  gap: 8px;
}

.newsletter-form input[type="email"] {
  flex: 1;
  padding: 12px 16px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 4px;
  font-size: 14px;
  outline: none;
}

.newsletter-form input[type="email"]:focus {
  border-color: #0070f3;
}

.newsletter-form button {
  padding: 12px 20px;
  background-color: #0070f3;
  color: white;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 4px;
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: bold;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background-color 0.2s;
}

.newsletter-form button:hover {
  background-color: #0051a8;
}

/* Responsive adjustment for mobile screens */
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .newsletter-form {
    flex-direction: column;
  }
}
```

---

### Option 2: No Backend? Use a Free Service
A plain HTML form needs a server to actually save the emails. If you don't have a backend set up yet, the easiest free options are:

1. **Formspree (Easiest for custom HTML):**
   * Go to [formspree.io](https://formspree.io) and get a free form endpoint.
   * Change the `<form>` tag in Option 1 to:
     ```html
     <form class="newsletter-form" action="https://formspree.io/f/YOUR_FORM_ID" method="POST">
     ```
   * Submissions will automatically be emailed to you or sent to a Google Sheet.

2. **Newsletter Platforms (Mailchimp, ConvertKit/Kit, Substack, Brevo):**
   * If you want to automatically send emails out later, create an account on one of these platforms.
   * Go to their dashboard, navigate to **Forms** -> **Create Form** -> **Embed**.
   * Copy their generated code snippet and paste it directly into your website's HTML.

---

### Want to make this tailored to your site?
Tell me:
1. What tech stack are you using? (e.g., WordPress, React/Next.js, Webflow, Shopify, plain HTML/CSS)
2. Where do you want the collected emails to go? (e.g., Mailchimp, a database, Google Sheets, or your email inbox)

